      "text_raw": "call this a parallel oscillator,\nalthough C is still 200 times\ns\nmore important than C for\np\nthe determination of the\noscillation frequency.\nThe point in the middle is\nthe crossover value f ,\nm\nbetween series and parallel\nresonance. Since at f we\np\nhad a pulling factor p of\nabout 0.25%, the point in\nthe middle must have a pull-\ning factor of about half or\n0.125%.\nWe can now conclude\nthat the pulling factor p\nmust be less than about\n0.1%, to have a oscillator with good stability and predictability!",
